# FAC-133 runtime containment artifacts (OS seatbelt needs abs paths ephemerally)
**/.herd/contain/
.herd/sessions/
**/.herd/sessions/

# FAC-133 control-plane state. SECRET-BEARING — never stage these:
#   .herd/control/mac.secret   HMAC secret (WriteControlMACSecret, every prod dispatch)
#   .herd/brokers/*.ctrl.json  control_token + host_creds ("Bearer $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", ...)
# The rest is durable runtime state (sealed envelopes, issuer sequence,
# readiness attestation, mailboxes) that is per-machine, never reviewable.
.herd/control/
**/.herd/control/
.herd/brokers/
**/.herd/brokers/
.herd/readiness/
**/.herd/readiness/
.herd/mail.jsonl
**/.herd/mail.jsonl
.herd/control-mail.jsonl
**/.herd/control-mail.jsonl
.herd/legacy-tab-state.jsonl

# compiled binaries must not be tracked
/herd
TASK-PACKET.md

# go test -c artifacts (never commit)
*.test

# Runtime SQLite state is created on demand and must never be committed.
# Broad pattern: named entries below kept drifting behind new runtime
# databases (launch-claims.db, claims.db, leases.db, and others were
# untracked-but-unignored, one accidental `git add -A` away from landing on
# main) as new .db files were added without a matching gitignore update.
.herd/*.db
.herd/*.db-*
**/.herd/*.db
**/.herd/*.db-*
.herd/reconciliation.jsonl
**/.herd/reconciliation.jsonl
.herd/legacy-tab-state.jsonl
**/.herd/legacy-tab-state.jsonl
.herd/command-sessions.db
.herd/container-lifecycle.db

# Runtime ledger and queue state. These are per-checkout operational files, not
# source: tracking them makes a live fleet's state a merge conflict, and an
# empty tracked copy would overwrite a real one on checkout. Two were swept in
# by a `git add -A` that ran after a command created them.
.herd/review-ledger.jsonl
.herd/harvest-queue.jsonl
.herd/review-ledger.jsonl.*
.herd/harvest-queue.jsonl.*

# FAC-711: review packets are RUNTIME artifacts. A packet records the exact
# worktree a reviewer was pinned to, so its contents legitimately contain an
# absolute path on this host -- and left untracked-and-unignored they failed the
# preflight boundary check inside `herd selftest`, exactly as the scout-planner
# guard receipts did in chainseer (CHA-3176).
#
# Ignoring PRESERVES them: they stay on disk as evidence and stay out of the
# repository. Same reasoning as .herd/coverage/ and .herd/bootstrap/ above.
.herd/review-packets/
.herd/review/
.herd/pool/
